Harden a Dockerfile and a Kubernetes Deployment manifest. The files are in `/tmp/exam/mhagou-006-q4/` (nothing has to be built or deployed): `Dockerfile` and `Deployment.yaml`.

1. `Dockerfile`:
   - every image stage must use a pinned Ubuntu version as its base image (for example `ubuntu:22.04`, not `latest`);
   - the containers must run as the `nobody` user instead of root: the final image stage must explicitly select `nobody` as its runtime user. The Dockerfile must still build: a step that needs root (such as installing packages) must still run as root.
2. `Deployment.yaml` (the Deployment `kafka`, do not rename it):
   - it must use the API version `apps/v1`;
   - no regular container and no init container may run in privileged mode;
   - every regular container and every init container must use a read-only root filesystem.
